# ThreadSanitizer suppressions. Keep this list short, and explain every entry.
#
# Asio's kqueue reactor (macOS) creates a descriptor_state on one thread and
# passes the pointer to another thread through the kevent() syscall. The kernel
# orders the write before the read, but TSan can't see through syscalls, so it
# reports a race on the state's mutex flag.
#
# The ^ anchor matters. TSan matches patterns against each frame's full
# demangled signature, parameter types included. Every Asio handler, ours too,
# runs under scheduler::do_run_one(conditionally_enabled_mutex::scoped_lock&, ...),
# so without the anchor this entry would hide real races in our handlers
# (checked by planting a race in AccessRequestHandler).
race:^asio::detail::conditionally_enabled_mutex::
